    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0885b537-c9f5-47f8-aa4f-0ad7bbebf412&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9207219124067_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Barn Manager",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Assistant Barn Manager Staff Full-Time Equestrian, Ashland, VA, US 2 days ago Requisition ID: 1727 Apply Salary: $40,000.00 Annually Randolph-Macon College invites applications for a full-time Assistant Barn Manager to join the Randolph-Macon College Equestrian Center. The Assistant Barn Manager supports the overall operation of the farm, including horse care, pasture and facility maintenance, and supervision of staff. This position works closely with professional staff, veterinarians, farriers, students, boarders, prospective students, and visitors. The ideal candidate has an outstanding working knowledge of horses and the operation of a professional show barn, a strong commitment to safety, and the ability to support the Barn Manager in maintaining a safe and well-run facility. The Center is located three miles from our Ashland campus, boasts 70 acres of pasture, has space for 56 horses, and includes an indoor riding arena, two large outdoor areas, and space for riding outside. Working Conditions Horse care is an ongoing responsibility that must be maintained throughout the year, including weekends, holidays, and during inclement weather. As a result, this position is considered essential personnel by the College and may require staff coverage or coordination outside normal business hours to ensure the health and safety of the horses. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Assistant Barn Manager will assist the Barn Manager in: Overseeing basic farm and pasture maintenance and supervising farm/stable workers, including creating and prioritizing daily tasks and responsibilities. Assisting with staff scheduling for full-time, part-time, and student workers and providing scheduling support in the absence of the Barn Manager. Monitoring horses for emergency wound care, lost shoes, injuries, illness, and other health concerns, including coordinating veterinary and farrier needs. Managing school horses and tending to their daily needs, including feed schedules, special dietary and care needs, pasture rotations, turnout schedules, and necessary veterinary and farrier services. Monitoring supplies and inventory, including feed, shavings, hay, and other barn supplies, and coordinating procurement and purchasing with the Barn Manager. Communicating professionally with boarders, College staff, outside vendors, hay and feed suppliers, farriers, veterinarians, students, prospective students, and visitors to the Equestrian Center. Performing and overseeing farm and facility maintenance, including dragging arenas, maintaining riding rings, cutting grass, and other necessary grounds and barn maintenance. Managing day-to-day safety and security measures and assisting with the preparation and management of horse shows and Equestrian Center events. Assisting the Barn Manager with maintaining accurate and up-to-date records for all horses and the overall daily operation of the Equestrian Center, including other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred. Prior experience managing or working in a professional barn environment required. Experience working with and handling horses required. Experience managing a top competition barn and top competition horses preferred. Exceptional knowledge of horse care and welfare, including the ability to learn the temperament of individual horses and recognize and respond appropriately to safety concerns. Veterinary knowledge and ability to administer IV and IM injections, perform wound care and bandaging, and provide other routine horse care. Ability to make effective decisions in emergency situations involving horses and humans. Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks based on general instructions, and demonstrate a strong work ethic. Strong communication and motivational skills, with the ability to work effectively and maintain positive relationships with students, co-workers, visitors, guests, and other members of the College community. Ability to operate several types of machinery, including tractors, front-end loaders, and post hole diggers, as well as drive a pick-up truck with trailer. Benefits Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Retirement plan with College match College Tuition Benefits Vacation, Sick, Personal, and Holiday Paid Time Off Parental Leave Life Insurance and AD&D Short-term and Long-term Disability benefits Wellness Programs The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has 1500 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capitol. Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application Please complete an online application at https://bit.ly/4hnWZrh to include uploading a resume, letter of interest, and contact information for two professional references addressed to: Claudia Burcham, HR Generalist. Screening of applications will begin immediately. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
