      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Join Our Talent Community Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL Custodian Housekeeping Staff Full-Time Physical Plant, Ashland, VA, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1695 Apply Salary: $16.00 Hourly Randolph-Macon College invites applications for a full-time Custodian to join our Custodial Team. Why work at Randolph-Macon College? Join a supportive campus community while enjoying a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision insurance, a College-matched retirement plan, tuition benefits, generous paid time off, parental leave, disability coverage, life insurance, and wellness programs. Responsibilities Cleaning of academic, administrative, and student housing areas. Qualifications High school diploma or GED and a valid driver’s license required with satisfactory motor vehicle record by insurance standards. Lifting or moving of materials up to 50lbs is required. Applicants with cleaning experience and familiarity with associated equipment is preferred. Schedule Monday - Friday, 6am-2:30pm. Required to be on-call one week out of the month. Position is deemed as Essential Personnel, requiring availability during emergency situations or periods of disruption. Comprehensive benefits package At Randolph-Macon College, we offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support you and your family, including: Medical, dental, and vision insurance Retirement plan with a College match College tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick, personal, and holiday leave Parental leave Employer-provided life insurance and AD&D coverage Short-term and long-term disability coverage Wellness programs and employee well-being resources The College Founded in 1830, Randolph-Macon has about 1800 students and is located in Ashland, VA, a residential community 15 miles north of Richmond and 90 miles south of Washington D.C., thereby having all the benefits for its students, faculty and staff of a dynamic metropolitan area which serves as the state capital.  Over 85% of students reside on campus. For more information about the College see www.rmc.edu . Randolph-Macon College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status in its education or employment programs or activities. Application To apply for the position, submit the following documents to https://bit.ly/49IYqMz in Microsoft Word or PDF format:  a current resume, cover letter addressing the position responsibilities and qualifications, and contact information for two professional references to Claudia Burcham, HR Generalist.  The review and interview process will commence as strong applications are received, and the search will remain open until the position is filled. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPl